URL:https://jackofthewood.com/events/bluegrass-jam-special-edition-featuri
 ng-the-darren-nicholson-band/
SUMMARY:BLUEGRASS JAM SPECIAL EDITION FEATURING THE DARREN NICHOLSON BAND
DESCRIPTION:\nA Grammy nominee and the winner of 13 International Bluegrass
  Music Association awards\, Darren Nicholson has taken his own brand of mo
 untain music around the world. A regular for years on the Grand Ole Opry a
 nd a founding member of acclaimed bluegrass group Balsam Range\, Darren no
 w spends his time recording\, writing new songs\, and performing original 
 roots music inspired by the history &amp\; culture of his native Western N
 orth Carolina —&nbsp\;homegrown\, wholehearted music with a purpose.\n\n
 \n\nA punchy mandolinist with instrumentation nods to Bill Monroe and Mart
 y Stuart\, Darren is also an introspective songwriter\, technical harmony 
 singer\, convincing lead vocalist\, and a man on a mission. His shows are 
 a tailored experience — genuine\, entertaining\, and an extended handsha
 ke to the community\, reflecting the fun-witted and approachable character
  formed in his raising.\n\n\n\nDarren’s passion is sharing raw\, honest-
 to-goodness\, quality music with his audience. Music that’s good for his
  soul and theirs too. “That’s all I want\,” says Darren. “I want t
 o be a positive part of other people’s lives with music\, you know? I wa
 nt to be an ambassador to roots music – tip my hat to the past while loo
 king forward at the same time. This music was intended to be played in a w
 ay that adds joy to the community. All I want is to restore that purpose\,
  not to complete a transaction.”&nbsp\;\n\n\n\nDarren says that when you
  come out to a show\, whatever you do\, please come talk afterward. “I
 ’m like Willie Nelson. ‘I don’t want fans\, I want friends.’ It’
 s a communal thing.”&nbsp\;\n\n\n\nJoining Darren on vocals are seasoned
  full-time band member AVERY WELTER (guitar) along with Avery’s former S
 hedhouse Trio partners SARAH GRIFFIN (upright bass) and BRADY WALLEN (banj
 o)\, both of whom are now full-time members of The Darren Nicholson Band a
 s well.\n\n\n\nThis expanded full-time lineup brings together a powerhouse
  of Appalachian musicians with deep roots in traditional bluegrass and a s
 hared passion for music\, reflecting Darren’s continuing commitment to e
 volving his approach to bluegrass.\n\n\n\n“I couldn’t be more thrilled
  . . . this means new sounds and new material. I can’t wait to see what 
 this new chapter holds. And I think folks who come out to see the new band
  will be as blown away by their music as I am.”\n\n\n\nThis newest itera
 tion of the band is rooted in the sounds of the Appalachian mountains yet 
 unafraid to explore new territory — with strong instrumental interplay\,
  distinctive vocal harmonies\, original material\, and the energy of four 
 musicians who are deeply connected to the music.\n\n\n\nDoors at 6pm —&n
 bsp\;show starts at 7pm. Suggested cover at the door. Open Jam follows at 
 9:30pm.\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/1WLUcPovyCY?si=aywqVKci4-9xcC3C\n\n\n\n\
 n\nhttps://youtu.be/ed8sKWA3CCQ?si=rjF1JGqa7dCv61yW\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://you
 tu.be/8QlDK2gCsLk?si=ZBXy3C8Y2Hjycp0I\n\n\n\n\n\nhttps://youtu.be/5oUJ-AP-
 20U?si=l_R6ciyESeMSgy3N\n\n
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://jackofthewood.com/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/09/10-22-26_BluegrassJam-DarrenNicholsonBand_IG_1080x1440.jpg
END:VEVENT
